<title>GERMANY: German state Baden-Wuerttemberg Jan CPI up 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>German state Baden-Wuerttemberg Jan CPI up 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The statistics office of the German state of Baden-Wuerttemberg reported the following consumer prices changes for January.</p>
<p>    Cost of living		   January	  December</p>
<p>    Mth/mth (pct change)	    +0.5		+0.2</p>
<p>    Year/year			   +1.7		+1.2</p>
<p>Note - These data are later combined with data from three other major German states to calculate the preliminary inflation figure for the whole of west Germany.  </p>
<p>The office gave the following breakdown of its cost of living data:</p>
<p>Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr   Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     +0.5	+1.7     114.9</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.3	+2.1     124.4</p>
<p> Household energy			  +2.0	+5.5     103.4</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  -1.3	+1.3     120.4</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  +0.5	+1.0     115.5</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods +0.1	+1.0     112.3</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   +1.3	+1.6     110.4</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   -0.5	+0.4     110.6</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.2	+2.5     113.1</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   +1.8	+2.4     115.0</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
